From: nixos-m4pro
Subject: [PATCH] Quiet start-up: no line for a missing environment or a deferred keyboard

With the environment nowhere (pkgs/u-boot.nix) there is nothing to load,
and the J614s MTP keyboard fails its first probe with -ENODEV only because
board_late_init starts it later. Neither needs a line on the screen.
---
--- a/env/env.c	2026-11-14 14:43:33.304120938 +0530
+++ b/env/env.c	2026-11-14 14:43:46.244608832 +0530
@@ -189,7 +189,9 @@
 		if (!env_has_inited(drv->location))
 			continue;
 
-		printf("Loading Environment from %s... ", drv->name);
+		/* Nothing to report when there is no stored environment. */
+		if (drv->location != ENVL_NOWHERE)
+			printf("Loading Environment from %s... ", drv->name);
 		/*
 		 * In error case, the error message must be printed during
 		 * drv->load() in some underlying API, and it must be exactly
@@ -197,7 +199,8 @@
 		 */
 		ret = drv->load();
 		if (!ret) {
-			printf("OK\n");
+			if (drv->location != ENVL_NOWHERE)
+				printf("OK\n");
 			gd->env_load_prio = prio;
 
 			return 0;
--- a/common/stdio.c	2026-11-14 14:43:33.306690773 +0530
+++ b/common/stdio.c	2026-11-14 14:43:46.244741040 +0530
@@ -316,7 +316,11 @@
 		for (ret = uclass_first_device_check(UCLASS_KEYBOARD, &dev);
 				dev;
 				ret = uclass_next_device_check(&dev)) {
-			if (ret)
+			/*
+			 * -ENODEV: not ready yet. The J614s MTP keyboard is
+			 * started later, by board_late_init ("mtpkbd start").
+			 */
+			if (ret && ret != -ENODEV)
 				printf("%s: Failed to probe keyboard '%s' (ret=%d)\n",
 				       __func__, dev->name, ret);
 		}
